# B6: a whole bug report, start to finish, by synthetic events through the real
# annotator and the real T window, with no window on the desktop. Photos and
# recordings go in the script's own out directory, never game/interchange:
#
#   cargo run --release -- --play scripts/b6-report.play --out out/play/b6-report --interchange out/play/b6-report --replays out/play/b6-report
#
# Then, in a fresh process, what an agent does with what it made:
#
#   cargo run --release -- --replay out/play/b6-report/b6-sand.replay --interchange out/play/b6-report
#
# The script does what Andrew would: start recording, walk, see something, F9,
# draw on the frame, say what's wrong, get back to the game, and at the end make
# the report. The words are the script's; the marks go through the same pointer
# events a hand makes.

# ---- a photo to annotate from the roll
mode fly
at -4.5654 117.4744 1500
look -60 -35
skytime 09:30
photo shot_hills_morning

# ---- record: flat ground, a pile of sand with its foot knocked out
find flat
assert find_kind == flat
replay record b6-sand.replay
assert recording == true
select 4
assert selected_block == sand
aim 3 0 0
tap place
aim 3 0 1
tap place
aim 3 0 2
tap place
aim 3 0 0.2
tap break
tick 14
assert edits > 0
aim 3 0 1
turn 8 2
settle

# ---- F9: pen, then a box, then words. The game stops.
assert steps > 0
mark
assert menu_annotating == true
assert menu_open == false
menu shot a01_open
mark stroke 0.66 0.44 0.70 0.42 0.74 0.44 0.75 0.49 0.72 0.53 0.68 0.53 0.65 0.49 0.66 0.44
menu click ink-yellow
menu click tool-box
mark stroke 0.29 0.49 0.57 0.71
menu click ink-blue
menu click tool-arrow
mark stroke 0.90 0.20 0.585 0.56
menu type The sand stack came down, and its top now sits above the line of the terrace
menu shot a02_drawn
menu key ctrl+z
menu shot a03_undone
menu click ink-blue
mark stroke 0.90 0.20 0.585 0.56
menu click tool-text
menu click canvas 0.60 0.12
menu type top of the stack
menu key enter
menu shot a04_text
menu key enter
assert menu_annotating == false
marked
assert mark_saved == true
assert mark_annotated == true
assert mark_marks == 4

# ---- on with the game: a second marker, cancelled and then kept
hold w 1
tap jump
mark
menu click tool-pen
mark stroke 0.2 0.2 0.3 0.3
menu key esc
assert menu_annotating == true
menu shot a05_esc_once
menu key esc
assert menu_annotating == false
marked
assert mark_saved == false
hold a 0.5
settle
mark
menu click tool-box
mark stroke 0.40 0.30 0.60 0.55
menu type Second look from further along
menu click annot-save
marked
assert mark_saved == true
wait 1
replay stop
assert replay_notes == 0
assert replay_markers == 2

# ---- it replays exactly, markers and all
replay check b6-sand.replay
assert replay_ok == true
assert replay_end_match == true
assert replay_look == same
assert replay_markers_read == 2

# ---- F9 with nothing recording: a marked photo in the roll
mark
menu click tool-pen
mark stroke 0.2 0.5 0.3 0.45 0.4 0.5
menu type Not recording: this one is a photo
menu key enter
marked
assert mark_saved == true

# ---- the T window: photos and recordings
menu open
menu wait
assert menu_photos == 2
assert menu_recordings == 1
menu shot m01_photos
menu click photo-1
menu wait
menu shot m02_photo_selected

# ---- annotate a photo from the roll
menu click annotate
menu wait
assert menu_annotating == true
mark stroke 0.60 0.30 0.66 0.36 0.72 0.31
menu type The ridge has a seam along here
menu shot m03_annotate_photo
menu click annot-save
assert menu_annotating == false
menu wait
assert menu_photos == 2
menu shot m04_marked

# ---- the recording: a title and description, its markers, and the report
menu click tab-recordings
menu wait
menu click rec-0
menu click rec-title
menu type Sand stack sits too high (example)
menu click rec-description
menu type An example made by scripts/b6-report.play. The words are the script's and this is not a real bug.
menu click rec-save
menu wait
menu click marker-0
menu wait
menu shot m05_recording
menu click make-report
menu shot m06_make_report
menu click report-go
menu wait
assert menu_report != none
menu shot m07_report_made

# ---- and a report of photos, ticked on the roll
menu click tab-photos
menu click tick-0
menu click tick-1
menu click report-photos
menu click report-title
menu type Two photos (example)
menu click report-go
menu wait
assert menu_report != none
menu close
